// src/user/compositor/xdg_shell_popup.pdx -- Wave0-B7-03 (paideia-os #2265)
//
// KIND_XDG_POPUP = 0x1C5, derived over KIND_WINDOW (paideia-os #2254 =
// G7-M3-001 / B6-05, landed in Wave-0 Batch-6).
//
// Design authority:
//   * design/compositor/pwp-spec-vocabulary.md §2.7 KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE
//     and KIND_XDG_POPUP -- the XDG-shell-equivalent surface pair. The
//     TOPLEVEL_STATE half landed at 0x1C4 in Batch-6 (B6-07,
//     xdg_shell_states.pdx / #2260); this row is the POPUP half of the
//     pair, and picks the adjacent slot 0x1C5 so the two XDG-shell rows
//     are contiguous.
//   * design/compositor/pwp-spec-vocabulary.md §3 derivation graph --
//     KIND_XDG_POPUP is a leaf under KIND_WINDOW, which itself derives
//     from KIND_SURFACE.
//
// PURPOSE. A derived-kind capability that names one popup surface
// anchored to a parent (a toplevel window or an earlier popup in the
// dismiss chain). Carries the anchor rectangle in the parent's local
// coordinate space, an anchor-edge / gravity pair naming WHERE the
// popup attaches on that rectangle and WHERE it grows from, an additive
// offset, and -- crucially -- a grab-seat binding for input capture
// plus a serial that gates the grab against a stale input event. Held
// per-popup by the toolkit; the compositor consumes it to drive
// popup-window placement, keyboard/pointer grab acquisition, and the
// dismiss chain when a click lands outside the popup stack.
//
// SEPARATION FROM KIND_WINDOW (spec §2.7). Popup semantics are a
// SEPARATE derived kind, not fields on KIND_WINDOW, so that a toolkit
// that composes windows without popup semantics (a tiling terminal
// mux, a headless render harness) can hold KIND_WINDOW without ever
// minting a popup cap. That factoring also lets the same window carry
// multiple concurrent popups (a menubar spawning a submenu spawning a
// tooltip) as three independent rows on one dismiss chain -- popup
// stacking is one-to-many over its parent, and one derived kind per
// popup is the cleanest way to spell that.
//
// NOVEL-CLEAN CHOICES.
//   * ANCHOR RECT IS IN PARENT-LOCAL SPACE. Not in output-local pixels,
//     not in root-window pixels: the rect is (x, y, w, h) inside the
//     parent's window geometry. The compositor materialises the parent
//     origin at popup-map time. This is what Wayland's xdg_positioner
//     converged on after xdg_shell v6 tried global pixel coords and
//     produced a class of "popup jumps when parent moves" bugs the
//     entire xdg-shell-v6-to-stable migration was written to close.
//   * GRAB IS TIED TO A SEAT + SERIAL. The mint gate refuses a grab
//     bound to a seat without a nonzero serial -- the serial is the
//     input event that AUTHORISED the grab. This mirrors Wayland's
//     xdg_popup.grab semantics and closes the "any client can steal
//     the pointer by minting a popup with a grab" class of bugs that
//     bit early Wayland compositors (and every X11 client-side popup
//     library). A popup WITHOUT a grab (seat_kind_id == 0) is legal
//     and describes a hover-tooltip / non-modal-menu case; the serial
//     field is ignored in that arm.
//   * DISMISS CHAIN IS EXPLICIT, NOT INFERRED. dismiss_parent_popup_
//     kind_id names the popup earlier in the chain (0 == this popup
//     is anchored directly on the toplevel). A dismiss event walks
//     THIS chain, not the parent-window chain -- so a popup spawned
//     from a submenu spawned from a menubar tears down cleanly on
//     an outside-click without extra bookkeeping in the compositor.
//     Wayland leaves the client responsible for computing the chain;
//     making it a first-class row field means the compositor's
//     dismiss handler is O(depth) with no client-side round trips.
//
// =============================================================================
// SLOT ALLOCATION -- KIND_XDG_POPUP = 0x1C5
// =============================================================================
//
// 0x1C5 is verified free at landing time by grep across src/ and
// design/. It sits adjacent to KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE at 0x1C4 (its
// XDG-shell sibling, landed B6-07) and immediately before KIND_CLIP_
// OFFER at 0x1C6 (B6-08). The Wave-0 Batch-6 dispatcher allocated
// 0x1B8..0x1C6 to the compositor vocabulary landings and left 0x1C5
// open for exactly this row -- the parenthetical comment in
// clipboard.pdx §"Section 1  Kind allocation" ("... 0x1C5 to sibling
// PWP-vocabulary kinds ...") names the reservation window; no live
// claim on 0x1C5 exists across src/ or design/.
//
// If a later refactor renumbers KIND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE off 0x1C4 or
// KIND_WINDOW off 0x1C1, the XPOP_PARENT_KIND constant below is the
// single reconciliation point (one-line edit + fingerprint re-emission).
//
// =============================================================================
// DERIVATION OVER KIND_WINDOW
// =============================================================================
//
// Parent kind is KIND_WINDOW (the G7-M3-001 landing; spec §2.4 makes
// WINDOW the toplevel-window authority and pins it as the parent of the
// TOPLEVEL_STATE / POPUP pair in §2.7). Mint requires the parent-window
// cap to carry R_WIN_MINT_XDG_POPUP (0x10000 in window_kind.pdx): only
// the process that authored the parent window (or a delegate holding a
// re-mint-carrying window cap) may create a popup for it. This mirrors
// the parent-carries-MINT gate every derived-kind in this tree uses.
// The kernel-side dispatch handler + parent-kind check lands as a
// follow-up milestone; this file is the SCHEMA SEED that registers the
// ordinal, publishes the row layout and rights bits, and exposes the
// pure schema helpers (factory, has-grab predicate, dismiss-chain
// accessor) every downstream landing will read from.
//
// =============================================================================
// ROW LAYOUT -- 64 BYTES (one cache line)
// =============================================================================
//
//   [+0]  header:      in_use[63:56] | reserved[55:0]
//   [+8]  popup_id:    u64, kernel-assigned monotonic, never 0
//   [+16] parent_pack: parent_window_kind_id[31:0] |
//                      grab_seat_kind_id[63:32]
//                      (grab_seat_kind_id == 0 means "no grab" --
//                      hover-tooltip / non-modal-menu case)
//   [+24] chain_pack:  dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id[31:0] |
//                      serial[63:32]
//                      (dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id == 0 means
//                      "anchored directly on the toplevel"; serial
//                      is the input-event serial that authorised
//                      the grab, ignored when seat == 0)
//   [+32] anchor_xy:   anchor_rect_x[31:0] (i32) | anchor_rect_y[63:32] (i32)
//   [+40] anchor_wh:   anchor_rect_w[31:0] (i32) | anchor_rect_h[63:32] (i32)
//   [+48] offset_xy:   offset_x[31:0] (i32) | offset_y[63:32] (i32)
//   [+56] edge_pack:   anchor_edge[7:0] | gravity[15:8] | reserved[63:16]
//
// ANCHOR COORDINATES ARE SIGNED (i32 per coord). Negative coordinates
// are permitted so an anchor rect that partially lies outside the
// parent's window geometry (as happens when a menubar's popup anchors
// at column 0 of a window whose left edge is off-screen after a drag)
// still round-trips cleanly through the pack/unpack pair.
//
// ANCHOR EDGE / GRAVITY ENUMS. Both use the same nine-value enumeration
// (NONE / TOP / BOTTOM / LEFT / RIGHT / TOP_LEFT / TOP_RIGHT /
// BOTTOM_LEFT / BOTTOM_RIGHT). anchor_edge names the point on the
// anchor rect the popup attaches to; gravity names the direction the
// popup grows from that attach point. E.g. anchor_edge = BOTTOM +
// gravity = BOTTOM makes a drop-down-menu; anchor_edge = RIGHT +
// gravity = RIGHT makes a submenu that fans right off a menu item.
//
// GRAB-SERIAL DISCIPLINE. When grab_seat_kind_id != 0, serial MUST be
// nonzero -- the mint gate refuses (XPOP_MINT_GRAB_NO_SERIAL). This is
// what prevents a client from stealing input by minting a popup on any
// seat: the client has to name a serial from a real input event it
// just received. The compositor's dispatch handler will additionally
// validate the serial against the seat's most-recent-event ledger; that
// cross-check is a follow-up milestone.

module XdgShellPopup = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1 -- KIND ORDINAL + PARENT + POOL CEILING
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let KIND_XDG_POPUP        : u64 = 0x1C5
  pub let XPOP_PARENT_KIND      : u64 = 0x1C1   // = KIND_WINDOW (B6-05, #2254)

  // Pool ceiling. 16 concurrent popup rows -- a nested menubar chain
  // (menubar -> menu -> submenu -> submenu -> tooltip) is at most five
  // deep, and a heavily-tabbed session with per-tab context menus rarely
  // holds more than a dozen popups live; 16 is the realistic ceiling
  // before the compositor should force a dismiss cascade. 16 * 64 =
  // 1024 bytes -- one 1 KiB slab, one cache-line-aligned per row.
  pub let XPOP_MAX       : u64 = 16
  pub let XPOP_ROW_BYTES : u64 = 64

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 2 -- RIGHTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Row-facing rights are addressable independently so a compositor
  // that hands a popup cap to a client for position-query only can
  // strip every write bit. Kernel-standard rights (R_XPOP_MINT /
  // R_XPOP_REVOKE / R_XPOP_OBSERVE) occupy the usual conventional bits
  // so a substrate that already knows those slots can dispatch without
  // a rights-table remap. Bit layout mirrors xdg_shell_states.pdx
  // exactly for cross-cap consistency: 0x001..0x008 = row-write /
  // row-read, 0x010 = revoke, 0x200 = mint, 0x400 = observe.

  pub let RIGHT_SET_POSITION    : u64 = 0x001
  pub let RIGHT_GRAB_INPUT      : u64 = 0x002
  pub let RIGHT_DISMISS         : u64 = 0x004
  pub let RIGHT_QUERY_POSITION  : u64 = 0x008
  pub let R_XPOP_REVOKE         : u64 = 0x010
  pub let R_XPOP_MINT           : u64 = 0x200
  pub let R_XPOP_OBSERVE        : u64 = 0x400
  pub let R_XPOP_ALL            : u64 = 0x61F  // 0x001|0x002|0x004|0x008|0x010|0x200|0x400

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3 -- ANCHOR-EDGE + GRAVITY ENUM
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Nine-value enumeration shared by both anchor_edge and gravity.
  // Ordinal values are stable and MUST NOT be renumbered -- they ride
  // the wire in the edge_pack word's low two bytes. A future revision
  // that added e.g. CENTER (a Wayland proposal that never landed) would
  // extend past 8, and every consumer of xdg_popup_edge_valid /
  // xdg_popup_gravity_valid would need to widen its predicate.

  pub let ANCHOR_NONE         : u64 = 0
  pub let ANCHOR_TOP          : u64 = 1
  pub let ANCHOR_BOTTOM       : u64 = 2
  pub let ANCHOR_LEFT         : u64 = 3
  pub let ANCHOR_RIGHT        : u64 = 4
  pub let ANCHOR_TOP_LEFT     : u64 = 5
  pub let ANCHOR_TOP_RIGHT    : u64 = 6
  pub let ANCHOR_BOTTOM_LEFT  : u64 = 7
  pub let ANCHOR_BOTTOM_RIGHT : u64 = 8
  pub let ANCHOR_MAX          : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 4 -- ROW LAYOUT OFFSETS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // These offsets are the machine-readable spelling of the row layout
  // documented in the file header. Every producer / consumer of a row
  // reads through THESE constants, not through hand-rolled +8 arithmetic.

  pub let XPOP_OFF_HEADER      : u64 = 0
  pub let XPOP_OFF_POPUP_ID    : u64 = 8
  pub let XPOP_OFF_PARENT_PACK : u64 = 16
  pub let XPOP_OFF_CHAIN_PACK  : u64 = 24
  pub let XPOP_OFF_ANCHOR_XY   : u64 = 32
  pub let XPOP_OFF_ANCHOR_WH   : u64 = 40
  pub let XPOP_OFF_OFFSET_XY   : u64 = 48
  pub let XPOP_OFF_EDGE_PACK   : u64 = 56

  // Sub-word offsets inside the packed words. Byte 0 of the edge_pack
  // word holds anchor_edge; byte 1 holds gravity. Named so a consumer
  // that only wants one byte can issue a targeted byte-load instead of
  // a full u64 unpack.
  pub let XPOP_EDGE_PACK_EDGE_BYTE    : u64 = 56   // = XPOP_OFF_EDGE_PACK + 0
  pub let XPOP_EDGE_PACK_GRAVITY_BYTE : u64 = 57   // = XPOP_OFF_EDGE_PACK + 1

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 5 -- OP TAGS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Kernel dispatch surface. Every op is arity-one from the caller's
  // perspective; op_arg semantics vary by op and are documented at each
  // op tag. Dispatch lands in a follow-up milestone.

  pub let XPOP_OP_SET_POSITION         : u64 = 0   // op_arg = positioner buffer ptr
  pub let XPOP_OP_GRAB_INPUT           : u64 = 1   // op_arg = seat kind_id (top 32 bits ignored)
  pub let XPOP_OP_DISMISS              : u64 = 2   // op_arg = 0
  pub let XPOP_OP_QUERY_POSITION       : u64 = 3   // op_arg = out ptr (6 i32s + 2 u8s)
  pub let XPOP_OP_QUERY_PARENT_WINDOW  : u64 = 4   // -> parent_window_kind_id
  pub let XPOP_OP_QUERY_GRAB_SEAT      : u64 = 5   // -> grab_seat_kind_id (0 = no grab)
  pub let XPOP_OP_QUERY_DISMISS_CHAIN  : u64 = 6   // -> dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id
  pub let XPOP_OP_QUERY_SERIAL         : u64 = 7   // -> serial
  pub let XPOP_OP_QUERY_POPUP_ID       : u64 = 8   // -> popup_id
  pub let XPOP_OP_DEBUG_PRINT          : u64 = 9   // R_XPOP_OBSERVE; row dump
  pub let XPOP_OP_MAX                  : u64 = 9

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 6 -- FAILURE TAXONOMY -- 0xFFFFEA70..0xFFFFEA7F
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // A fresh 16-wide band verified free at landing time by grep across
  // src/ and design/. Sits below the surface_commit block
  // (0xFFFFEA60..0xFFFFEA6F, B6-02) and above the KIND_WINDOW block
  // (0xFFFFEAA0..0xFFFFEAAF, B6-05); the intervening pages
  // 0xFFFFEA80..0xFFFFEA9F are reserved for sibling B6 landings and
  // remain available for other B7 batch rows to pick from.

  pub let XPOP_OK                      : u64 = 0
  pub let XPOP_TAIL_ENOSPC             : u64 = 0xFFFFEA7F
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_PARENT         : u64 = 0xFFFFEA7E
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_RIGHTS         : u64 = 0xFFFFEA7D
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_EDGE           : u64 = 0xFFFFEA7C
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_GRAVITY        : u64 = 0xFFFFEA7B
  pub let XPOP_MINT_GRAB_NO_SERIAL     : u64 = 0xFFFFEA7A  // seat != 0 && serial == 0
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_ANCHOR         : u64 = 0xFFFFEA79
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_SEAT           : u64 = 0xFFFFEA78
  pub let XPOP_MINT_BAD_CHAIN          : u64 = 0xFFFFEA77
  pub let XPOP_BAD_SLOT                : u64 = 0xFFFFEA76
  pub let XPOP_BAD_RIGHTS              : u64 = 0xFFFFEA75
  pub let XPOP_WRONG_KIND              : u64 = 0xFFFFEA74
  pub let XPOP_REVOKE_ALREADY          : u64 = 0xFFFFEA73
  pub let XPOP_UNSUP_OP                : u64 = 0xFFFFEA72
  pub let XPOP_BAD_ARG                 : u64 = 0xFFFFEA71
  pub let XPOP_ROW_NONE                : u64 = 0xFFFFEA70

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 7 -- STATS COUNTER SLOTS
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // The kernel-side substrate will publish a _xpop_stats [u64; 8] table
  // in a follow-up milestone; the slot indices are named here so cross-
  // module bumpers agree.

  pub let XPOP_ST_MINTS         : u64 = 0
  pub let XPOP_ST_REVOKES       : u64 = 1
  pub let XPOP_ST_GRABS         : u64 = 2   // grab acquisitions
  pub let XPOP_ST_DISMISSES     : u64 = 3   // dismiss-chain walks
  pub let XPOP_ST_POSITION_SETS : u64 = 4   // successful set_position calls
  pub let XPOP_ST_REFUSED       : u64 = 5
  pub let XPOP_ST_MAX           : u64 = 8

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 8 -- FINGERPRINT (one line, legacy-suffixed)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Emitted once on successful mint by the future substrate. The
  // legacy-suffix convention is what tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh
  // enumerates, so this literal is the machine-checkable name of the
  // milestone. No fingerprint on the set / query / revoke paths.
  pub let pdx_kind_xdg_popup_meta : [u8; 46] = "xdg popup mint ok [legacy: XDG POPUP MINT OK]\0"

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 9 -- VALIDATORS (pure leaves, small immediates)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Every function in this section is a pure unsafe-bodied leaf with
  // small immediates, returns in rax, and clobbers only rax + one
  // scratch. No `test`, no `add reg, [mem]` -- per issue's coding
  // budget. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_ per row's reserved-label
  // discipline.

  // xdg_shell_popup_edge_valid(e) -> 1 iff e in [0, ANCHOR_MAX].
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_edge_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (e: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): anchor_edge validator. Admits 0..8 (NONE through BOTTOM_RIGHT). Small immediate so no MOVABS. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_ev_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 8;
        ja  xdg_shell_popup_ev_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_ev_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_gravity_valid(g) -> 1 iff g in [0, ANCHOR_MAX].
  // Same enumeration as anchor_edge; separate helper name so a call
  // site is self-documenting about which field it is validating.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_gravity_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (g: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): gravity validator. Admits 0..8 (same enumeration as anchor_edge). Small immediate so no MOVABS. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_gv_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 8;
        ja  xdg_shell_popup_gv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_gv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_u32_valid(v) -> 1 iff v <= 0xFFFFFFFF. Used for
  // every u32-shaped kind_id field the row layout stores (parent
  // window, grab seat, dismiss-parent popup).
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_u32_valid : (u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (v: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): u32 range validator. 0xFFFFFFFF as `mov r10, imm32` sign-extends to all-ones which is exactly the mask we want (ja against it admits any 32-bit value). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_uv_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        cmp rdi, r10;
        ja  xdg_shell_popup_uv_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_uv_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_grab_valid(seat, serial) -> 1 iff (seat == 0) OR
  // (seat != 0 AND serial != 0). THE grab-discipline gate. A popup
  // without a grab (seat == 0) is legal (hover-tooltip case); a popup
  // WITH a grab MUST cite a nonzero input serial so the compositor can
  // cross-check against the seat's most-recent-event ledger. Uses
  // `cmp reg, 0` + branches -- no `test`.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_grab_valid : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (seat: u64) (serial: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): grab-discipline gate. seat == 0 -> pass (no grab); seat != 0 AND serial == 0 -> fail (unauthorised grab); seat != 0 AND serial != 0 -> pass. No `test`; branches on `cmp reg, 0` + `je`/`jne`. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_gr_.",
      block: {
        cmp rdi, 0;
        je  xdg_shell_popup_gr_ok;      // no grab -> pass
        cmp rsi, 0;
        je  xdg_shell_popup_gr_no;      // grab with no serial -> fail
      xdg_shell_popup_gr_ok:
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_gr_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 10 -- PACKERS
  // ==========================================================================

  // xdg_shell_popup_parent_pack(parent_window_kind_id, grab_seat_kind_id)
  // -> parent[31:0] | seat[63:32]. Both fields masked to 32 bits before
  // the shift so an out-of-range argument cannot smear into a neighbour.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_parent_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (parent_window_kind_id: u64) (grab_seat_kind_id: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): pack parent[31:0] | seat[63:32] per row layout at [+16]. Both fields masked to 32 bits with 0xFFFFFFFF (`mov r64, imm32` sign-extends 0xFFFFFFFF to all-ones; correct as an AND mask). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_pp_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        mov rax, rsi;                    // seat
        and rax, r10;
        shl rax, 32;
        mov r11, rdi;                    // parent
        and r11, r10;
        or  rax, r11;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_chain_pack(dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id, serial)
  // -> dismiss[31:0] | serial[63:32]. Mirror of _parent_pack; separate
  // name to keep call sites self-documenting.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_chain_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id: u64) (serial: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): pack dismiss[31:0] | serial[63:32] per row layout at [+24]. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_cp_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        mov rax, rsi;                    // serial
        and rax, r10;
        shl rax, 32;
        mov r11, rdi;                    // dismiss_parent_popup
        and r11, r10;
        or  rax, r11;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_i32_pair_pack(lo, hi) -> lo[31:0] | hi[63:32].
  // Signed-coord pair packer used for anchor_xy, anchor_wh, and
  // offset_xy: the low 32 bits of each argument are taken verbatim,
  // sign bit included, so a negative coord round-trips correctly
  // through the pack/unpack pair.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_i32_pair_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (lo: u64) (hi: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): signed i32 pair pack -- lo[31:0] | hi[63:32]. Used for anchor_xy at [+32], anchor_wh at [+40], offset_xy at [+48]. Low 32 bits taken verbatim so a negative i32 round-trips (interpreted as u32 in the wire word, re-interpreted as i32 by the reader). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_ip_.",
      block: {
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        mov rax, rsi;                    // hi
        and rax, r10;
        shl rax, 32;
        mov r11, rdi;                    // lo
        and r11, r10;
        or  rax, r11;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_edge_pack(edge, gravity) -> edge[7:0] |
  // gravity[15:8] | reserved[63:16]. Both fields masked to 8 bits.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_edge_pack : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn (edge: u64) (gravity: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): pack edge[7:0] | gravity[15:8] per row layout at [+56]. Reserved [63:16] left zero. Both fields masked to 8 bits so an out-of-range argument cannot smear. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_ep_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, rsi;                    // gravity
        and rax, 0xFF;
        shl rax, 8;
        mov r10, rdi;                    // edge
        and r10, 0xFF;
        or  rax, r10;
        ret
      }
    }

  // xdg_shell_popup_hdr_pack() -> canonical row header (in_use bit
  // set by the mint gate's tail_alloc, not here). Mirror of
  // xdg_shell_states's _hdr_pack: returns 0 today.
  pub let xdg_shell_popup_hdr_pack : () -> u64 !{} @{} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): canonical row header. Only in_use is ever written (by tail_alloc), low 56 bits stay 0. Mirrors xdg_shell_states.pdx xdg_shell_states_hdr_pack. Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_hp_.",
      block: {
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 11 -- FACTORY: xdg_popup_mint
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Writes the popup fields into an already-allocated row. Does NOT
  // allocate a row (that is the mint gate's job in a follow-up
  // milestone) and does NOT bump any counters (the substrate's dispatch
  // handler owns counter updates). Validates anchor_edge, gravity, and
  // the grab-discipline invariant (seat != 0 => serial != 0) before any
  // store; refuses the write on failure and leaves the row untouched.
  //
  // Signature: (row_ptr, parent_pack, chain_pack, anchor_ptr,
  //             offset_pack, edge_gravity_pack) -> u64
  //   * row_ptr:            pointer to a 64-byte row already tail-allocated
  //   * parent_pack:        parent_window_kind_id[31:0] | grab_seat_kind_id[63:32]
  //   * chain_pack:         dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id[31:0] | serial[63:32]
  //   * anchor_ptr:         pointer to 4 packed i32s -- [ax, ay, aw, ah]
  //                         (same 16-byte shape xdg_toplevel_state_set
  //                         uses for its geometry buffer)
  //   * offset_pack:        offset_x[31:0] (i32) | offset_y[63:32] (i32)
  //   * edge_gravity_pack:  anchor_edge[7:0] | gravity[15:8]
  //   * returns:            XPOP_OK on success; XPOP_MINT_BAD_EDGE /
  //                         BAD_GRAVITY / GRAB_NO_SERIAL on validation
  //                         failure; row is untouched on failure.
  //
  // Six args -- fits in SysV registers rdi..r9 with no stack spill.
  // Caller responsibility: pre-pack parent/chain/edge_gravity via the
  // packer helpers in Section 10; pre-populate anchor_ptr with four
  // i32s. The mint gate wrapper (kernel-side, follow-up) handles the
  // full parent-cap-carrying-R_WIN_MINT_XDG_POPUP check, the row-pool
  // allocation, and the counter bumps.
  pub let xdg_popup_mint : (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_ptr: u64) (parent_pack: u64) (chain_pack: u64) (anchor_ptr: u64) (offset_pack: u64) (edge_gravity_pack: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): factory that writes all popup fields into an existing row. Validates anchor_edge in [0,8], gravity in [0,8], and the grab-discipline invariant (seat != 0 => serial != 0) before any store. Uses `cmp reg, imm`+`ja`/`je`/`jne` -- never `test`. Six args fit in SysV rdi..r9. Scratch registers: rax, r8, r9, r10, r11 (all caller-saved); r8/r9 are the incoming offset_pack + edge_gravity_pack respectively and get consumed before being clobbered as scratch. No clobber of rbx/rbp/r12-r15 (SysV callee-saved). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_pm_.",
      block: {
        // ---- Validate anchor_edge (edge_gravity_pack[7:0]). ----
        mov r10, r9;                     // edge_gravity_pack
        and r10, 0xFF;                   // edge byte
        cmp r10, 8;
        ja  xdg_shell_popup_pm_bad_edge;

        // ---- Validate gravity (edge_gravity_pack[15:8]). ----
        mov r10, r9;
        shr r10, 8;
        and r10, 0xFF;                   // gravity byte
        cmp r10, 8;
        ja  xdg_shell_popup_pm_bad_gravity;

        // ---- Grab-discipline: if seat != 0 then serial != 0. ----
        // seat  = parent_pack >> 32  (rsi)
        // serial = chain_pack >> 32  (rdx)
        mov r10, rsi;                    // parent_pack
        shr r10, 32;                     // seat
        cmp r10, 0;
        je  xdg_shell_popup_pm_grab_ok;  // no grab -> serial ignored
        mov r11, rdx;                    // chain_pack
        shr r11, 32;                     // serial
        cmp r11, 0;
        je  xdg_shell_popup_pm_no_serial;
      xdg_shell_popup_pm_grab_ok:

        // ---- All validated. Commit the writes. ----

        // parent_pack -> row_ptr[+16].
        mov [rdi + 16], rsi;

        // chain_pack -> row_ptr[+24].
        mov [rdi + 24], rdx;

        // Anchor xy from anchor_ptr[0..8] -> row_ptr[+32].
        mov r10d, [rcx + 0];             // ax (i32; zero-extended as u32)
        mov r11d, [rcx + 4];             // ay
        shl r11, 32;
        or  r10, r11;
        mov [rdi + 32], r10;

        // Anchor wh from anchor_ptr[8..16] -> row_ptr[+40].
        mov r10d, [rcx + 8];             // aw
        mov r11d, [rcx + 12];            // ah
        shl r11, 32;
        or  r10, r11;
        mov [rdi + 40], r10;

        // offset_pack -> row_ptr[+48].
        mov [rdi + 48], r8;

        // edge_pack write: edge[7:0] | gravity[15:8] | reserved[63:16].
        // We take the low 16 bits of edge_gravity_pack verbatim (both
        // bytes have been validated above) and mask to 16 bits so the
        // reserved [63:16] bits stay zero.
        mov r10, r9;
        and r10, 0xFFFF;
        mov [rdi + 56], r10;

        xor rax, rax;                    // XPOP_OK = 0
        ret;

      xdg_shell_popup_pm_bad_edge:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEA7C;             // XPOP_MINT_BAD_EDGE
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_pm_bad_gravity:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEA7B;             // XPOP_MINT_BAD_GRAVITY
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_pm_no_serial:
        mov rax, 0xFFFFEA7A;             // XPOP_MINT_GRAB_NO_SERIAL
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 12 -- PREDICATE: xdg_popup_has_grab(row_ptr) -> bool
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Returns 1 if the row's grab_seat_kind_id is nonzero (the popup
  // holds an input grab), 0 otherwise. Reads the parent_pack word at
  // row_ptr + 16 and inspects the high 32 bits.
  pub let xdg_popup_has_grab : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): predicate returning 1 iff grab_seat_kind_id (parent_pack[63:32]) is nonzero. `cmp reg, 0` + `je`/`jne` (no `test`). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_hg_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 16];             // parent_pack
        shr rax, 32;                     // seat
        cmp rax, 0;
        je  xdg_shell_popup_hg_no;
        mov rax, 1;
        ret;
      xdg_shell_popup_hg_no:
        xor rax, rax;
        ret
      }
    }

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 13 -- QUERY: xdg_popup_dismiss_chain(row_ptr) -> u64
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Returns the dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id, i.e. the popup earlier
  // in the dismiss chain. 0 means "this popup is anchored directly on
  // the toplevel" (equivalent to Option::None for the caller). A
  // compositor's dismiss handler walks the chain by iterating this
  // accessor until it returns 0.
  pub let xdg_popup_dismiss_chain : (u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_ptr: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "G7-M4-003 (#2265): read dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id from chain_pack[31:0] at row_ptr + 24. AND with 0xFFFFFFFF (loaded via `mov r64, imm32` which sign-extends but AND truncates correctly). Returns 0 when this popup is toplevel-anchored (chain root). Labels prefixed xdg_shell_popup_dc_.",
      block: {
        mov rax, [rdi + 24];             // chain_pack
        mov r10, 0xFFFFFFFF;
        and rax, r10;                    // dismiss_parent_popup_kind_id
        ret
      }
    }
}
